  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish temperature-dependent mechanical testing of closely related FCC HEAs, temperature-sensitive dislocation strengthening and deformation-mode transitions, FCC/HCP and stacking-fault mediation, nanoscale molecular-dynamics deformation, and elevated-temperature wear testing of an HEA film. R15 is especially relevant because it predicts suppression of stacking faults as temperature rises in CoCrFeMnNi. However, none describes the specific FeNiCrCoCu/Cu coating architecture or combines temperature-controlled nanoindentation and friction simulation with a high-temperature transition to lattice disorder, dislocation-density loss, softening, and increased friction. An expert would be pointed toward the general question, but selecting and explaining the later paper's specific intervention would require a substantial additional idea."
